      "en": "Growing towns, commerce and states in the Ganga valley accompanied questions about suffering, conduct and rebirth. Siddhartha Gautama attained enlightenment at Bodh Gaya and first taught at Sarnath. Mahavira is regarded as the twenty-fourth Jain Tirthankara, not the first. The Buddhist sangha organised monks and nuns; lay supporters contributed donations. Both traditions emphasise ethical conduct and liberation, but their teachings are not identical."
